{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["Your right hand, YHWH — is You." "Nordari be-koach — is It." "You shatter the enemy — 'Your right hand' (yemincha) is in the feminine, as written: ימין ה׳ רוממה. And this verse in Tehillim: נשאו נהרות ה׳ נשאו נהרות קולם. עד מתי רשעים ה׳ עד מתי רשעים יעלוזו. כי הנה אויביך ה׳ כי הנה אויביך יאבדו — its first half does not complete its statement until the second half comes and repeats it and completes the statement. But in the first half it mentions whom it is speaking of."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {2 "The lemma 'נאדרי בכח' (Exodus 15:6) is transliterated rather than translated in entry 1 because Rashbam's comment 'היא' ('it is [feminine]') identifies the grammatical subject, and the lemma's form itself is the point. The unaddressed Tehillim verses are from Psalm 93:3–4 (נשאו נהרות) and Psalm 94:3–5 and 92:10 (כי הנה אויביך), cited without addresses as is Rashbam's custom; they are left unaddressed per instructions. The punctuation and verse divisions in the quoted Psalm sequence are inherently ambiguous."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:35.054007085Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}